{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-cs-evaluation-faithfulness","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:cs-evaluation-faithfulness","kind":"proposition","title":"Faithfulness of the Chern--Simons evaluation on the brane tower","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-volume-tower-decomposition","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-yekutieli-lifting"],"tags":["chern-simons","yekutieli","faithfulness","obstruction","brane-tower"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful","text":"cs-evaluation-faithfulness.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:cs-evaluation-faithfulness\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_n(K)</code> denote the tower-level volume contribution from the <a href=\"#prop:volume-tower-decomposition\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-open-problems\">tower decomposition</a>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_n \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code> denote the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-th <a href=\"#def:quantum-characteristic-classes\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting-construction\">quantum characteristic class</a>.</p>\n<p>The Chern--Simons evaluation map is <em>faithful</em> at each tower level. For every hyperbolic knot or link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> in the Descartes spectrum,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\kappa_n \\neq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\Phi_n(K) \\neq 0.</code></pre>\n<p>If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_n</code> defines a non-trivial obstruction in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code>, the Chern--Simons period integral over the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-th twisted sector yields a non-zero real contribution to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Vol}(K)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/cs-evaluation-faithfulness.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"16.17.2","page":"b/prop-cs-evaluation-faithfulness","qa":{"counts":{"pass":86,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
